## Initial Q&A
### Was the UK government publishing separate weekly surveillance reports on influenza (flu) and COVID-19 prior to October 2020?
Answer: Yes, based on the search result, the UK government was publishing separate weekly surveillance reports on influenza (flu) prior to October 2020. The source lists a collection titled "weekly national flu reports" with entries dating back to at least the 2018 to 2019 season, and notes that reports from spring 2013 and earlier are archived. However, the result does not explicitly mention separate weekly COVID-19 reports before October 2020, only that combined "National flu and COVID-19 surveillance reports" were added later.

Source URL: https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/weekly-national-flu-reports

### Did the UK government or a UK public health authority combine its weekly influenza surveillance report and its weekly COVID-19 surveillance report into a single combined report?
Answer: Yes, the UK public health authority Public Health England (PHE) combined its weekly influenza and COVID-19 surveillance reports into a single document, as evidenced by the "Weekly National Influenza & COVID-19 Report" for week 41 (with data up to week 40, October 2020).

Source URL: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5f7f354b8fa8f51e7b9dc623/Weekly_Flu_and_COVID-19_report_W41_FINAL.pdf

